course: dictionary
lesson: 9951
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Peel back the husk and each long silky thread leads to one kernel.» Here the threads are on a corn cob, not on a cushion.
explain: Tassel is one of these words. Its first meaning is a bunch of loose threads tied together at the top, used to decorate cushions, curtains or hats. Its second meaning is the tuft of flowers at the top of a maize (corn) plant.
explain: How do you tell which one is meant? Read the words around it. «Pollen from the feathery tassel on top must land on that silk» is about a plant, because pollen and silk belong to maize flowers. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A tassel is a bunch of threads or strings tied together at the top, hanging loose at the bottom.
fact: Tassels are used for decoration on cushions, curtains, hats, scarves and bookmarks.
fact: On a maize (corn) plant, the tassel is the tuft of flowers at the top of the stem.
fact: «Pollen from the tassel must land on the silk for that kernel to grow.»
fact: Each silk thread on a maize cob is joined to one kernel, so pollen must reach plenty of silk.
exercise: «Each silk thread on a maize cob is joined to one kernel.» What is a tassel in a maize plant? | A kind of seed inside the cob | *The tuft of flowers at the top of the plant | A bunch of loose threads on a cushion | A long green leaf
exercise: Mia's new cushion has a tassel on each corner. What is a tassel here? | A flower that grows on a maize plant | A kind of kernel | *A bunch of threads tied together at the top and hanging loose | Pollen that falls on silk
exercise: «Pollen from the feathery tassel on top must land on the silk.» Which word tells you the tassel is part of a plant? | scarf | cushion | bookmark | *pollen
test: Ravi hangs a tassel from his school bag. What is it? | A green stem | Pollen that falls on silk | A corn cob full of kernels | *A bunch of loose threads tied together at the top
test: «Maize is planted in blocks so pollen reaches plenty of silk.» What does the tassel of a maize plant do? | *Makes pollen that falls on the silk below | Joins to one kernel and grows into a seed | Hangs loose from the corner of a cushion | Holds the husk closed
exam: «The silky tassel hung down from the edge of the cushion.» Which sentence uses tassel with the same meaning? | *The tassel on her scarf swung as she walked | Each tassel is one kernel on the cob | The tassel on the top of the maize plant makes pollen | The tassel was full of kernels
